  "meaning": "The whole-roster theorem supplies one actual concrete necessary root. The imported supplied-root convergence helper identifies every maximum, if any, with this same root. Under the existing God-is-maximal-in-being converse, every God candidate therefore equals that root, so any two God candidates equal each other. This proves the existing at-most-one GodIsOne statement, not God existence or uniqueness of all necessary individuals. No maximum-existence, grades, CauseMore, pure-act, simply-prior or forward God-naming premise is used. All nine listed premises remain open commitments except the separately recorded logical floor; no independent philosophical premise is discharged.",
